caption: High Magic Parameters
tradition-component: high-magic-parameters

Damage: 1d6 per 2 full points of margin of success.

Healing: 2d6 per 3 points of margin of success.

Unless a parameter below gives a local High Magic conversion, use the applicable GURPS Thaumatology Appendix A table and read the result directly from the working’s margin of success.

Range: Use the applicable table.

Mass: Use the applicable table.

Targets: Use the applicable table.

Area: Use the applicable table.

Duration: Use the applicable table.

Range in Time: Use the applicable table, but only for sensory effects or future triggers; High Magic cannot travel through time.

Granted Traits: 10 character points per point of margin of success.

Use the vanilla GURPS syntactic-magic resistance rules. The GM determines whether a working is Resisted; almost any direct Body or Mind effect should be, while effects that deal direct physical damage generally are not. For a Resisted High Magic working, use the lowest-margin required Word roll as the caster’s side of the resistance contest. Rolled attacks and constructs are resolved through normal attack, active-defense, and DR rules rather than an additional resistance roll against their damage.
